# Interpreter-throw closure item 2 (steps/interpreter-throw-20261010.md): the interpreter fault of a walked callee passes
# through a NATIVE caller with no declared names and no handler, and reaches the root uncaught: R0 stops with the
# implicit ordinal of a callee declaring no names, interpreter = 4 (before: the "callable that cannot throw" abort).
fn: bad (int: n) int
    return: 12 / n

fn: relay (int: n) int
    int: native_probe c.abs(n)
    return: bad(n)

int: result relay(0)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
